---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, HOST_NAME, CATEGORY, ARTWORK, AARON_IMAGES } from '../lib/site';

const description = `About ${SITE_NAME} — a podcast of conversations with people engaged in their own self-healing, hosted by ${HOST_NAME}.`;

const structuredData = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: HOST_NAME,
    jobTitle: 'Host and creator',
    worksFor: { '@type': 'CreativeWorkSeries', name: SITE_NAME },
    url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description={description}
  path="/about/"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Our Healing Voices</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A podcast of conversations with humans who are engaged in their own self-healing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell shell-narrow page">
    <section aria-labelledby="show-heading">
      <h2 id="show-heading">The show</h2>
      <div class="show">
        <div class="show__text">
          <p>
            Our Healing Voices is a podcast hosted and created by {HOST_NAME}. Each episode is a
            conversation with a person who is engaged in their own healing — someone willing to
            describe what they have lived through, what it cost, and what they are still working on.
            The subjects follow the people: grief, love, the body, family and relationships,
            parenthood, resilience, purpose, spirituality, transformation, the Earth.
          </p>
          <p>
            The show is listed under {CATEGORY}, but it is not a programme of advice. There is no
            method being taught here and no outcome being promised. There are people, and there are
            the stories they are willing to tell about their own lives.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="show__art">
          <img
            src={ARTWORK.src}
            alt={ARTWORK.alt}
            width={ARTWORK.width}
            height={ARTWORK.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="why-heading">
      <h2 id="why-heading">Why these conversations</h2>
      <p>
        Healing is not a subject people usually get to speak about at length. It happens in private,
        it takes years, and it rarely arrives in the shape anyone planned for. What this show offers
        is time and a willing listener — long enough for someone to say the whole thing rather than
        the summary.
      </p>
      <p>
        The recurring phrase behind the show is <strong>LOVE &amp; HEAL</strong>. That is the
        orientation: love for people, and respect for the fact that healing is something a person
        does themselves, on their own terms and at their own pace. What one guest found may be
        nothing like what the next one found. Both accounts are worth hearing.
      </p>
      <p>
        So the site is built around people and stories rather than around episode numbers. You can
        start with a guest, or with a theme that sounds like something you are carrying, and follow
        it into the next conversation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="perspective-heading">
      <h2 id="perspective-heading">Perspective</h2>
      <p>
        These conversations are held with curiosity rather than authority. Aaron is not a doctor, a
        therapist, or a person with the answers, and the show does not present itself that way.
        Guests speak for themselves. Their experience is theirs, described in their own words, and it
        is not offered as a prescription for anyone else.
      </p>
      <Disclaimer />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="aaron-heading">
      <h2 id="aaron-heading">{HOST_NAME}</h2>
      <div class="host">
        <figure class="host__figure">
          <img
            src={AARON_IMAGES.portrait.src}
            alt={AARON_IMAGES.portrait.alt}
            width={AARON_IMAGES.portrait.width}
            height={AARON_IMAGES.portrait.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            sizes="(min-width: 52rem) 18rem, 100vw"
          />
        </figure>
        <div class="host__text">
      <p>
        Aaron is in awe of humans. He says so plainly, and it is the clearest description of why this
        show exists. He is drawn to people who are healing, to people who care deeply about the
        Earth, and to people who love people — and his part of the conversation is mostly listening.
      </p>
      <p>
        He has also turned the microphone on himself. Episodes about grief that has not finished,
        about new fatherhood, about sleepless nights and endless love, are his own. He is a host who
        is also inside the subject, which is part of why guests seem willing to go where they go.
      </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    background: var(--surface-mist);
    padding-block: var(--space-l);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .intro h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .page {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .show {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  .show__art img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 20rem;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .host {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .host__figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .host__figure img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 18rem;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .host__text > :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .host {
      grid-template-columns: 18rem 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-l);
    }

    .show {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 20rem;
      gap: var(--space-l);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
